    "proseHtml": "<p class=\"lead\">Dalby is the commercial hub of the Western Downs, a serious agricultural centre that sits where the grain, cotton and cattle country meets the energy industry of the Surat Basin. It's a busy town with one of the country's larger cattle saleyards and a steady flow of freight tied to farming and gas. Road Linx Transport delivers into Dalby, running the Warrego Highway corridor from Brisbane through Toowoomba and out to the Western Downs.</p><p>For a town that both produces and services major industries, reliable freight over the range is essential, and we run that route regularly.</p><h2>Freight for grain, cattle and gas country</h2><p>Dalby's economy is broad. It's a grain and cotton centre, a major cattle town, and a service base for the Surat Basin coal seam gas industry. That mix means freight of every kind, from agricultural inputs, packaging and equipment to materials and supplies for the energy sector.</p><p>We carry it with the right equipment, from tautliners and semi-trailers for palletised and bulk freight to flat-tops and drop-decks for machinery, materials and oversize loads. Tail-lift trucks handle deliveries to farms and sites without a forklift, which is the norm out here.</p><h2>Direct along the Warrego corridor</h2><p>Dalby is west of Toowoomba on the Warrego Highway, and we run the whole corridor from Brisbane. Freight comes up the range and out to Dalby on the one carrier, so it stays on a single truck rather than being handed off partway. That direct link keeps Dalby connected to Brisbane, the Port and the coast for both incoming supplies and outgoing goods.</p><h2>Full loads and combined runs</h2><p>We handle full loads out to Dalby and can also combine smaller consignments into a planned run along the corridor, so whether you're sending a whole trailer or a few pallets, there's an efficient way to move it.</p><h2>Trailer hire and delivery to site</h2><p>Dalby deliveries go to farms, yards, sites and shopfronts, so our tail-lift trucks lower heavy freight to ground level where there's no forklift. Our semi-trailer hire gives local operations extra capacity through busy seasons, and we run early morning and after-hours deliveries to suit agricultural and industrial schedules. It all runs under Chain of Responsibility on load-rated restraint, with a signed POD on request for the record.</p><h2>Areas we cover around Dalby</h2><p>We service Dalby and the surrounding Western Downs, along the Warrego Highway corridor. From Dalby we connect east to Oakey, Toowoomba, Brisbane and the Port, and west to Chinchilla and the Surat Basin towns.</p><h2>Servicing the Surat Basin from Dalby</h2><p>Dalby's growth over the past decade has been tied to the Surat Basin gas fields as much as to its long-standing farming base. That energy activity has added a steady demand for materials, equipment and supplies staged through the town and out to sites across the region.</p><p>We carry that alongside the agricultural and general freight Dalby has always moved, including the goods tied to its major saleyards. Running the corridor from Brisbane and Toowoomba, we keep Dalby connected whether the freight is bound for a farm, a site or a business in town.</p><p>Dalby is a working hub, not a quiet country town, with saleyard days and gas-sector movements adding to the usual farm freight. We plan runs that fit around that activity, so deliveries land without getting tangled in the town's busy periods.</p><p>Dalby runs one of the largest cattle selling centres in the country, and the activity around it ripples through the town's freight task. Sale days, farm supply and gas-sector movements all share the same roads, and we plan Dalby runs to work around that rhythm so deliveries land cleanly rather than fighting the busiest hours.</p>",
