    "proseHtml": "<p class=\"lead\">Lismore is the commercial heart of the inland Northern Rivers, a service centre for a wide farming region and a university city on the Richmond River. It's also a city that has been rebuilding, and that recovery has driven real demand for building materials and freight. Road Linx Transport delivers into Lismore and the surrounding district, running goods down from Brisbane and the Gold Coast.</p><p>We understand that freight into Lismore isn't just business as usual for many customers, so we treat it with the reliability the rebuild deserves.</p><h2>Supplying a rebuilding region</h2><p>The 2022 floods hit Lismore hard, and the recovery since has kept a steady flow of building materials, trade supplies and equipment moving into the city and the surrounding villages. Alongside that, Lismore's long-standing role as an agricultural service centre and a base for Southern Cross University keeps ordinary commercial freight ticking over.</p><p>We carry the range, from timber, steel and trade materials for the rebuild to palletised stock and general freight for local businesses. Flat-tops and drop-decks handle the building materials and oversize loads, while tautliners and utes cover palletised and everyday freight.</p><h2>Direct runs down from Brisbane</h2><p>Lismore sits inland from the coast, and we run it as part of our Northern NSW corridor. Freight comes down direct from Brisbane and the Gold Coast on our own trucks, so it stays on one vehicle rather than being handed to linehaul and held at a depot. For a region that needs materials on site to keep rebuilding, that reliability matters.</p><h2>Tail-lift for sites without lifting gear</h2><p>A lot of Lismore deliveries go to sites, shopfronts and premises that don't have a forklift, including properties still being fitted back out. Our tail-lift trucks lower heavy and palletised freight to ground level safely, so a delivery doesn't depend on lifting equipment being available at the other end. It all runs under Chain of Responsibility on load-rated restraint, with signed PODs for the record when materials land on site.</p><h2>Connecting Lismore across the Northern Rivers</h2><p>Lismore is central to the inland Northern Rivers, and we link it with the coast and the wider region. From Lismore we run out to Ballina and the coast, north to Tweed Heads, the Gold Coast and Brisbane, and across the surrounding Northern NSW towns. A business supplying the region gets one carrier covering the spread.</p><h2>Areas we cover around Lismore</h2><p>We service Lismore, South Lismore, Goonellabah, Alstonville, Wollongbar, Casino and the surrounding Richmond Valley district. From here we connect to Ballina and the coast, north to the Gold Coast and Brisbane, and across the broader Northern NSW region.</p><h2>Reliability the recovery counts on</h2><p>When a region is rebuilding, freight reliability stops being a background detail. A trades crew waiting on materials, or a business trying to reopen, can't afford a delivery that turns up two days late or gets stuck at a depot somewhere between Brisbane and the Richmond Valley.</p><p>That's the standard we hold Lismore freight to. Direct runs, one truck, dependable timing, so the materials and stock the recovery depends on actually arrive when they're meant to. It's a small thing on paper and a big thing when you're the one waiting on site.</p><p>Lismore sits inland off the highway, and knowing the local roads matters when materials are heading to a specific site or street in the recovery. Our drivers run the district regularly, so deliveries reach the right spot without a detour.</p><p>Weather is a real factor inland, and local road knowledge counts when conditions turn. Our drivers run the Richmond Valley regularly and know which routes hold up, so a wet stretch doesn't have to mean a missed delivery to a Lismore site or a village out past Goonellabah.</p>",
    "proseStyle": null,
