    "proseHtml": "<p class=\"lead\">Oakey sits on the Warrego Highway just west of Toowoomba, a Darling Downs town where agriculture and defence sit side by side. It's home to a large beef processing operation and the Army Aviation Centre, and it's surrounded by the feedlots and farms that define this stretch of the Downs. Road Linx Transport delivers into Oakey, connecting the town with Toowoomba, Brisbane and the coast.</p><p>Being just off the main western highway, Oakey is a natural stop on our Darling Downs runs, and we service it as part of that route rather than as an afterthought.</p><h2>Freight for the Downs</h2><p>Oakey's economy runs on agriculture. The district is feedlot and farming country, with beef processing a major local employer, so freight here means everything from livestock-related inputs and packaging to processed product heading to market. There's also the steady trade and general freight that any working country town needs.</p><p>We carry the range with the right gear, from tautliners and semi-trailers for palletised and bulk loads to flat-tops for machinery and materials. Tail-lift trucks handle the deliveries to farms and sites without a forklift, which is common out this way.</p><h2>On the Warrego Highway route</h2><p>Oakey is a short run west of Toowoomba, and we fold it into our Darling Downs corridor. Freight comes up the range from Brisbane to Toowoomba and out along the Warrego to Oakey, all on the one carrier, so goods stay on a single truck rather than being handed off. That direct link keeps Oakey connected to Brisbane, the Port and the coast.</p><h2>Urgent runs when needed</h2><p>When an Oakey business or property needs something from Toowoomba or Brisbane in a hurry, our hot shot service can run a dedicated truck out along the highway, so an urgent part or delivery arrives the same day rather than waiting.</p><h2>Getting freight onto farms and yards</h2><p>Oakey deliveries often go to farm gates, sheds and yards with no forklift, so our tail-lift trucks lower heavy freight to ground level safely. Our semi-trailer hire gives local operations extra capacity when they need it, and we run early morning and after-hours deliveries to suit farm and processing schedules. Loads are secured to rating under Chain of Responsibility on load-rated equipment, with PODs available on delivery.</p><h2>Areas we cover around Oakey</h2><p>We service Oakey and the surrounding Downs district, along the Warrego Highway corridor between Toowoomba and the western towns. From Oakey we connect east to Toowoomba, Brisbane and the Port, and west to Dalby and Chinchilla.</p><h2>Defence, processing and farm freight</h2><p>Oakey is an unusual mix for a Downs town. Alongside the farms and feedlots there's a major beef processing operation and the Army Aviation Centre, and each brings its own freight into and out of the district.</p><p>We service that spread as part of our Warrego runs, from farm and processing supplies to general trade and commercial freight for the town itself. Being on the corridor between Toowoomba and the western Downs, Oakey is a natural stop for us rather than an out-of-the-way detour.</p><p>Oakey sits right on the Warrego Highway, which makes it an easy, regular stop rather than a detour. That position keeps freight to and from the town cost-effective, since it slots into runs already heading west or back to Toowoomba.</p><p>The Warrego Highway is the main east-west freight artery for this part of Queensland, and Oakey sits right on it. That keeps the town firmly on the route between Toowoomba and the western Downs, so freight in and out of Oakey rides established runs rather than one-off trips out of the way. The upshot for local businesses is dependable timing and a sharper rate than a town sitting off the main highway would ever get.</p>",
