    "proseHtml": "<p class=\"lead\">The Port of Brisbane at Fisherman Islands is where a huge share of Queensland's import and export freight lands, and getting it off the wharf and moving is its own discipline. Road Linx Transport runs landside cartage from the Port, moving cleared freight from the container terminals and empty container parks out to warehouses and customers across Brisbane and beyond.</p><p>If your goods have just come through the Port and need to be somewhere else quickly, this is freight we handle every week.</p><h2>From the wharf to your warehouse</h2><p>Once a container is cleared, the clock usually starts ticking on detention and storage. We move quickly to collect from the terminals along Port Drive and the surrounding precincts, then run the freight direct to your premises so you're not racking up avoidable charges.</p><p>For a lot of importers the smart move is straight-line delivery. Rather than send cleared stock to a depot to be broken down, we carry it directly from the Port to your dock or your customer's, handled once, which is faster and gentler on the freight.</p><h2>Container and palletised freight</h2><p>Port work isn't only containers. We handle the freight after it comes out of the box too, moving palletised import stock onward as general freight, distribution runs or B2B deliveries. That means one company can take your goods from the Fisherman Islands terminals all the way to the retailer or site they're destined for.</p><h2>Short-notice and time-critical runs</h2><p>Port timing rarely lines up neatly with business hours. When a container clears late or a slot opens up, we keep capacity for short-notice cartage, including early morning and after-hours collection, so your freight moves the moment it's ready rather than sitting another day.</p><h2>The right equipment for landside freight</h2><p>Depending on how your freight is packed and where it's going, a Port run might use a tautliner for palletised import stock, a flat-top for machinery or oversize items craned off, or a tail-lift truck for a delivery point with no forklift. All of it runs load-rated restraint under Chain of Responsibility, so heavy Port freight is secured properly for the road.</p><h2>Connecting the Port to the region</h2><p>Freight landing at Brisbane doesn't always stay in Brisbane. We run cleared Port freight out to the Gold Coast, the Sunshine Coast, Toowoomba and the Darling Downs, and south across the border into Northern NSW. So an importer bringing goods through Fisherman Islands can have them delivered to a customer in Yatala or Toowoomba on the same carrier that pulled them off the wharf.</p><h2>Areas we serve from the Port</h2><p>We cover the Port precincts at Fisherman Islands and Pinkenba, the nearby TradeCoast estates at Hemmant, Murarrie and Eagle Farm, and onward across Greater Brisbane and the wider South East Queensland and Northern NSW region. Wherever your cleared freight needs to land, we can carry it there direct.</p><h2>Working in with your clearance timing</h2><p>Every importer's timing is a little different, and the landside run has to flex around it. A container might clear customs first thing, or it might sit in quarantine inspection for the seasonal brown marmorated stink bug period and clear late in the day. We work in with whatever your clearance throws up rather than forcing your freight into a fixed slot.</p><p>We can also help with the tail end of the container cycle, returning empty boxes to the nominated park once you've unpacked. That closes the loop so you're not left arranging a separate movement for the empty.</p><p>Turnaround is everything on the wharf. The faster a cleared box is collected and unpacked, the less you spend on detention and storage, so we treat Port collections as time-sensitive by default rather than fitting them in around other work.</p>",
    "proseStyle": null,
    "faq": {
      "heading": "Port of Brisbane Transport & Cartage — answered",
      "items": [
        {
          "q": "Do you collect containers from the Port of Brisbane?",
          "a": "Yes. We collect cleared freight from the container terminals and precincts at Fisherman Islands and run it direct to your warehouse or customer, including moving palletised stock onward once it's out of the container."
        },
        {
          "q": "Can you help avoid container detention charges?",
          "a": "We move quickly once your container is cleared, collecting from the Port and delivering direct rather than via a depot, which helps you keep within detention and storage timeframes. Tell us your cut-offs and we'll plan around them."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do you run after-hours Port collections?",
          "a": "Yes. Port timing doesn't keep business hours, so we keep capacity for short-notice and after-hours cartage. When a container clears late or a slot opens, we can collect and deliver without waiting for the next day."
        },
        {
          "q": "Can you deliver Port freight outside Brisbane?",
          "a": "Yes. We carry cleared Port freight across South East Queensland and into Northern NSW, including the Gold Coast, Sunshine Coast, Toowoomba and the Darling Downs, so import stock can go straight from the wharf to a regional customer."
        },
        {
          "q": "What trucks do you use for Port cartage?",
          "a": "We match the truck to the freight: tautliners for palletised import stock, flat-tops for craned or oversize items, and tail-lift trucks for delivery points without a forklift, all under load-rated restraint."
        },
        {
          "q": "Can you take freight straight from the Port to my customer?",
          "a": "Yes. Direct Port-to-customer delivery avoids an extra depot stop for freight that's already been handled enough. We carry it once, from Fisherman Islands to your customer's dock, as a B2B run."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do you handle both import and export freight?",
          "a": "Our main Port work is landside cartage of cleared import freight to warehouses and customers, and we can also carry freight to the precincts for export handling. Tell us the movement and we'll confirm."
        },
        {
          "q": "Is my Port freight tracked?",
          "a": "Yes. We track cartage runs through our transport management system and provide signed PODs on delivery, so you have a clear record from the Port to the destination."
        },
        {
          "q": "How do I book Port of Brisbane cartage?",
          "a": "Call 07 3179 7072 or email admin@roadlinxtransport.com.au with the terminal, your delivery address and timing. We'll confirm the truck and price and move as soon as your freight is cleared."
        },
        {
          "q": "Can you return empty containers after unpacking?",
          "a": "Yes. Once your container is unpacked we can return the empty to the nominated container park, so you don't have to arrange a separate movement or risk running past the dehire date."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do you handle freight during the stink bug inspection season?",
          "a": "Yes. Seasonal quarantine inspections can delay clearance, and we plan around them, collecting as soon as your container is released rather than holding you to a fixed booking time."
        },
        {
          "q": "How quickly can you collect a cleared container?",
          "a": "We prioritise Port collections and can often be on the wharf the same day a container clears, so you keep within detention windows rather than paying avoidable charges."
        },
        {
          "q": "Can you deliver Port freight to multiple sites?",
          "a": "Yes. Once freight is off the wharf we can run it to several destinations as a planned multi-drop, or straight to a single customer, whichever suits your consignment."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do you carry oversize or heavy machinery from the Port?",
          "a": "Yes. For heavy or oversize items craned off at the terminals we use flat-tops and drop-decks, restrained to rating, and can advise on any over-dimension requirements."
        }
      ]
    },
