    "proseHtml": "<p class=\"lead\">The Sunshine Coast has grown from a string of beach towns into one of Queensland's fastest-moving regional economies, and that growth runs on reliable freight. Road Linx Transport delivers across the coast, from the industrial base at Kunda Park through Maroochydore and Kawana to Caloundra in the south and Noosa in the north.</p><p>We connect the coast to Brisbane too, running the Bruce Highway corridor so local businesses aren't cut off from their southern suppliers and customers.</p><h2>Freight for a growing coast</h2><p>Kunda Park is the coast's industrial heart, home to trade suppliers, manufacturers and distributors, and it generates a steady flow of freight. Beyond it, the region's building boom keeps materials moving to sites from Sippy Downs to Peregian, while a large hospitality and retail sector needs constant restocking through Maroochydore, Mooloolaba and Noosa.</p><p>We carry the lot. Palletised stock and trade materials for the Kunda Park businesses, building supplies to the coast's many construction sites, and delivery runs to the cafes, shops and venues that the coast is known for. Utes handle the quick jobs and semi-trailers take the full loads.</p><h2>The Brisbane to Sunshine Coast corridor</h2><p>The run up the Bruce Highway is a regular for us. We carry freight direct between Brisbane and the coast on our own trucks, so your goods stay on one vehicle the whole way with no depot handling. For coast businesses that rely on Brisbane suppliers, and Brisbane businesses supplying the coast, that direct link keeps timing predictable.</p><h2>Urgent runs when the coast can't wait</h2><p>Being a couple of hours from Brisbane, the coast sometimes needs something in a hurry. Our same-day hot shot service runs a dedicated truck straight up the highway, so an urgent part or order gets there today rather than on the next scheduled run.</p><h2>Tail-lift and after-hours for coast businesses</h2><p>Coast deliveries often go to shopfronts, cafes and fit-outs with no forklift, so our tail-lift trucks bring heavy freight down to ground level safely. And because hospitality and retail can't always take stock mid-trade, we run early morning and after-hours drops so venues from Caloundra to Noosa are restocked before they open. Every load is restrained to rating on load-rated equipment under Chain of Responsibility, and we close each drop with a POD when you want one.</p><h2>Areas we cover on the Sunshine Coast</h2><p>We service the whole region, including Kunda Park, Maroochydore, Kawana, Buderim, Sippy Downs, Caloundra, Mooloolaba, Coolum, Nambour, Noosa and the hinterland. From the coast we run south to Brisbane and the Port, and connect through to the Gold Coast and beyond when freight needs to travel further.</p><h2>Freight for the coast strip and the hinterland</h2><p>The Sunshine Coast is really two markets. There's the coastal strip from Caloundra to Noosa, and there's the hinterland around Nambour, Maleny and the growth corridors inland. Freight patterns differ between them, and we cover both rather than sticking to the easy coastal runs.</p><p>That matters as the region spreads inland. New estates and businesses opening up around Palmview, Sippy Downs and the hinterland towns need the same reliable supply as the established coastal centres, and we service them as part of the one network.</p><p>The coast is a couple of hours north of Brisbane, so a well-timed run matters. We plan pickups to suit the Bruce Highway rather than leaving freight to chance in traffic, which keeps delivery times predictable for coast customers.</p><p>The region's growth has a health and education backbone too, with the university and the hospital precinct at Birtinya anchoring the Kawana growth corridor. Precincts like that draw steady supply freight for fit-out, equipment and consumables, and we service them alongside the retail and construction runs that the coast is better known for.</p>",
    "proseStyle": null,
