    "proseHtml": "<p class=\"lead\">Toowoomba sits at the top of the range as the gateway between Brisbane and Queensland's west, and that position makes it one of the state's key freight towns. Road Linx Transport runs freight and transport in and out of Toowoomba, connecting the Darling Downs to Brisbane, the Port and the coast.</p><p>We know the range run, the local estates at Charlton and Torrington, and the way freight moves through this part of the world, so your goods get where they're going without fuss.</p><h2>Freight for the Darling Downs</h2><p>Toowoomba and the surrounding Downs are built on agriculture, and the freight reflects it. Machinery and inputs heading out to farms, produce and processed goods coming back, and a busy trade and construction sector supplying a growing regional city all keep trucks moving.</p><p>We carry palletised freight, trade materials and general goods across the region, with utes for local runs and semi-trailers for full loads. The Charlton and Torrington industrial areas, along with the freight precinct out toward Wellcamp, are regular stops for us.</p><h2>Over the range to Brisbane</h2><p>The run between Toowoomba and Brisbane is the lifeline for a lot of local businesses, and it's a regular for us. With the Toowoomba Second Range Crossing taking heavy freight around the city, the trip down to Brisbane and the Port is more reliable than it used to be, and we run it direct on our own trucks so your freight isn't handed off or held at a depot.</p><h2>Same-day and urgent range runs</h2><p>When a Downs business needs something from Brisbane in a hurry, or a Brisbane supplier has to get stock up the range today, our hot shot service runs a dedicated truck straight through. It's the fast option when a scheduled run won't cut it.</p><h2>Local delivery, trailer hire and out-of-hours runs</h2><p>Toowoomba deliveries range from farm gates to shopfronts, so our tail-lift trucks handle the drops without a forklift, and our semi-trailer hire gives local businesses extra capacity through busy periods without buying trucks. We also run after-hours and early morning deliveries where a business needs stock outside its trading day. Loads are restrained to rating under Chain of Responsibility, and a signed POD comes back with every delivery on request.</p><h2>Gateway to the west</h2><p>Toowoomba is where South East Queensland meets the west, and freight moving to or from the Surat Basin and the western Downs often passes through it. We connect Toowoomba with Oakey, Dalby and Chinchilla out along the Warrego Highway, so goods can move between Brisbane and the western towns on a single carrier that knows the route.</p><h2>Areas we cover in and around Toowoomba</h2><p>We service Toowoomba and its industrial areas at Charlton, Torrington and Wilsonton, the Wellcamp freight precinct, and the surrounding Darling Downs. From here we run east down the range to Brisbane and the Port, and west along the Warrego Highway to Oakey, Dalby and Chinchilla.</p><h2>The Wellcamp precinct and the road west</h2><p>Toowoomba's freight role has grown with the Wellcamp precinct out to the west of the city, which has added air freight and a purpose-built logistics hub to the region's road links. It reinforces what Toowoomba already was, the pivot point between the coast and the west.</p><p>We tie the city's road freight in with that wider picture, connecting Toowoomba businesses back to Brisbane and the Port in one direction and out to the Surat Basin towns in the other. For a regional centre that both consumes and forwards freight, having a carrier that runs both directions keeps things simple.</p><p>The climb up the range shapes every Toowoomba run. With the Second Range Crossing taking heavy freight around the city, our trucks reach the Downs more reliably than the old route allowed, which steadies timing in both directions.</p>",
    "proseStyle": null,
